{"body":"## Business Context & Purpose\n\nThe `rad-artifact` CLI can record where artifacts live (via `locate`) but cannot actually fetch them. Users must manually copy URLs and use external tools (curl, wget) to download artifacts. Adding a separate `rad-fetch` binary closes this gap — users can retrieve artifacts by CID from registered locations, with content integrity automatically verified.\n\nThe design uses a `Fetcher` trait to dispatch by URL scheme, supporting HTTP(S) and iroh-blobs out of the box, with easy extensibility for future protocols.\n\n## Expected Behavior/Outcome\n\n```\nrad-fetch <oid> <cid> [-o output] [--url <url>] [--repository <RID>]\n```\n\n- Looks up the release by OID, finds the artifact by CID\n- Collects URLs from registered locations (or uses `--url` override)\n- Tries each URL in order until one succeeds\n- Verifies downloaded content against the CID (sha2-256 for HTTP; iroh verifies BLAKE3 natively)\n- Writes to output path (defaults to artifact name in cwd)\n- Warns on stderr if the artifact is redacted\n\n## Architecture\n\n**Separate crate and binary.** The download functionality lives in `radicle-artifact-fetch` (under `fetch/`) with its own binary (`rad-fetch`), so users of the COB library (`radicle-artifact`) don't pull in networking dependencies (ureq, iroh-blobs, tokio, sha2). The `rad-artifact` CLI remains unchanged.\n\n**Workspace layout:** Root `Cargo.toml` gets `[workspace]` with members `[\".\", \"fetch\"]`.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n- **Trait-based dispatch.** A `Fetcher` trait with a `schemes()` method lets a registry pick the right handler per URL. Simple `Vec<Box<dyn Fetcher>>`.\n- **Two built-in fetchers:** `HttpFetcher` (ureq, sync) and `IrohBlobFetcher` (iroh-blobs, async bridged via `tokio::runtime::Runtime::block_on()`).\n- **Iroh locations as custom URLs.** Stored as `iroh-blob:<blake3-hash>@<node-id>` in the existing `locations` field.\n- **CID verification for HTTP only.** Iroh downloads skip CID verification since iroh-blobs verifies BLAKE3 integrity natively during transfer.\n- **Try URLs in order.** Use `all_locations()` to get every registered URL, try each until one succeeds.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### 1. Convert to workspace\n\nAdd `[workspace]` to root `Cargo.toml` with members `[\".\", \"fetch\"]`.\n\n### 2. New crate: `fetch/`\n\n**Library (`fetch/src/lib.rs`):**\n\n- `Fetcher` trait with `schemes()` and `fetch()` methods\n- `NeedsVerification` enum (`Yes` / `No`) returned by `fetch()`\n- `HttpFetcher` — `https`/`http` via `ureq`, returns `NeedsVerification::Yes`\n- `IrohBlobFetcher` — `iroh-blob` scheme, parses URL, bridges async via `block_on()`, returns `NeedsVerification::No`\n- `verify_cid(data, expected_cid)` — sha2-256 → multihash → CIDv1 (raw codec 0x55) → compare\n- `download(urls, expected_cid, dest, fetchers)` — tries URLs in order, verifies CID when needed\n- `default_fetchers()` — returns `[HttpFetcher, IrohBlobFetcher]`\n- `FetchError` enum: `UnsupportedScheme`, `Http`, `Iroh`, `Io`, `CidMismatch`, `InvalidIrohUrl`, `NoLocations`, `AllFailed`\n\n**Binary (`fetch/src/main.rs`):**\n\n- Clap-derived CLI mirroring `rad-artifact` style\n- Loads profile, opens repo, finds release by OID, looks up artifact by CID\n- Warns on stderr if redacted\n- Calls `download()` with `default_fetchers()`\n- Writes to output path, prints path to stdout\n\n### 3. No changes to `rad-artifact`\n\nThe existing COB library and CLI binary are untouched.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rad-fetch <oid> <cid>` fetches artifact from registered HTTPS locations\n- [ ] `rad-fetch <oid> <cid>` fetches artifact from `iroh-blob:` locations\n- [ ] Downloaded content verified against CID hash for HTTP downloads\n- [ ] `--output` flag allows specifying custom output path\n- [ ] `--url` flag allows overriding registered locations with a direct URL\n- [ ] Warning printed to stderr when downloading a redacted artifact\n- [ ] `FetchError::CidMismatch` returned when HTTP content doesn't match expected CID\n- [ ] `Fetcher` trait is extensible — new protocols can be added without modifying existing code\n- [ ] `cargo build --workspace`, `cargo test --workspace`, `cargo clippy --workspace` all pass\n- [ ] `radicle-artifact` crate has no new dependencies\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n- `Cargo.toml` — add `[workspace]` section\n- `fetch/Cargo.toml` — **new** — crate manifest\n- `fetch/src/lib.rs` — **new** — Fetcher trait, HttpFetcher, IrohBlobFetcher, CID verification, download logic\n- `fetch/src/main.rs` — **new** — `rad-fetch` CLI binary","embeds":[],"id":"dfc1acb4daf8ce818d6d92fc9ec8d49f42bdd039","type":"comment.edit"}